## User preferences

- when defining scanner behavior, the user required it “везде, включая ячейки, склад, сортировку, подбор отгрузки, подбор ФБС и инвентаризацию” -> make scanner support a cross-flow operator contract, including boxes, pallets, cargo places, and products, rather than a screen-local add-on. [Task 1] [skysight memory]
- for inventory, the user specified: scan a container, then product scans write factual quantities into that container; scan a product outside a container, otherwise prompt to scan its container -> preserve this explicit state machine in UI and tests. [Task 1] [skysight memory]
- before a near-term demo, the user pressed for what is really implemented, on staging, and adequately tested -> report mockup, local implementation, CI, staging, and live-browser acceptance separately; do not let urgency turn an observed status into a release claim. [Task 3] [skysight memory]
- for outbound picking, the user rejected a place-first presentation and required visual nesting that shows a box on a pallet -> keep the top level product-first and make the physical hierarchy genuinely legible, not merely encoded in a text label. [Task 4] [skysight memory]

## Reusable knowledge

- The observed audit distinguished barcode existence from usable scanner UI: packing and FBS picking reportedly had backend scan support but no scanner UI; receiving used a legacy custom scanner; Cyrillic-layout protection was reported only in that old receiving path, not shared `ScannerField`. A safe completion plan is shared backend recognition plus shared Cyrillic handling, then scanner UI in packing/FBS picking, and only then a risk-managed receiving migration. This plan was not source-verified. [Task 1] [skysight memory]
- Keep modal draft/comment state local while typing if map-wide rerenders cause input lag; the observed claimed fix avoided recalculating/rerendering the large draggable map on every character. Recheck the implementation and regression behavior before reuse. [Task 1] [skysight memory]
- Reconcile an apparent physical shortage with the current order allocation before calling it loss. In the observed table, active orders covered every missing row except `6720-6T` size `29` (counted 16, system 17, missing 1, current orders 0); uncounted rows and an overwritten `6720-5A` size-28 figure remained data-quality caveats. [Task 2] [skysight memory]
- The narrow A/B test attributed a material portion of slow pytest to repeated database setup: `tests/test_marking_pools_read.py` was observed at 9 passed in 10.84s with the revised setup versus 22.67s old. Treat this as a targeted benchmark, not full-suite/staging proof. [Task 3] [skysight memory]
- FBS order visibility and stock availability are separate: use the seller warehouse carried by `wb_warehouse_id` and its mapping to the FF warehouse to choose whose orders the operator sees; show unmapped warehouses as unresolved rather than hiding them. Do not infer owner/visibility from stock availability. [Task 4] [skysight memory]
- In product-first outbound picking, expand each product into actual storage places while retaining legible loose-stock, pallet, box, cargo-place, and nested box-on-pallet relationships; container-level write-off/movement is a stated requirement. The observed work was a local mockup, not live flow evidence. [Task 4] [skysight memory]
- Inventory is a draft before posting and should not mutate stock; calculate discrepancy at posting from current stock, warn when system stock changed since recount, and never treat uncounted rows as factual zero. Posting creates stock movements. [Task 5] [skysight memory]

## Failures and how to do differently

- Symptom: scanner support is called complete because objects have barcodes or a backend endpoint exists. Cause: recognition, keyboard-layout handling, and screen-level scanner UI were conflated. Fix: test each named workflow on real scanner/keyboard input, including a container-then-product inventory sequence and an unexpected item. [Task 1] [skysight memory]
- Symptom: a count difference is called a warehouse shortage. Cause: the comparison omits goods in active orders, uncounted rows, or ambiguous handwritten values. Fix: add current-order quantity to every discrepancy row, identify genuine residuals, and physically check the packing zone before loss/write-off action. [Task 2] [skysight memory]
- Symptom: a passing PR or fast targeted test becomes “ready for staging/demo.” Cause: CI, local test performance, deployment, and real operator browser flow are different evidence layers. Fix: report each layer explicitly and run proportional targeted checks without claiming skipped acceptance. [Task 3] [skysight memory]
- Symptom: a partially counted inventory displays a false shortage. Cause: uncounted rows are included as zero. Fix: keep uncounted distinct from fact quantity, block/flag calculation until the operator resolves the gap, and retain the current-stock-change warning at posting. [Task 5] [skysight memory]

